# cppcheck suppressions.  Each entry names a finding that is correct about the
# code and wrong about the intent; anything not listed here is a real report.
# Prefer an inline `// cppcheck-suppress <id>` with a reason when the exception
# is local to one line - this file is for the ones that are project-wide.
# Syntax is <id>[:<file glob>[:<line>]].
# EDITING RULE: never leave a line holding nothing but "#", anywhere in this
# file, including this header.  cppcheck skips a comment line only when it is
# longer than one character, then strips everything from the first "#" - which
# leaves an empty id and aborts the entire run with
#     cppcheck: error: Failed to add suppression. No id.
# Blank lines are skipped correctly, so use those as separators.

missingIncludeSystem
missingInclude

# Public API.  A library exists to be called from outside this repository, so
# "nothing in this tree calls it" is not a defect.
unusedFunction

# Suppressions that happen not to fire are expected: this list covers several
# build configurations and only one is checked per run, and cppcheck versions
# disagree about which findings exist.
unmatchedSuppression

# "Consider using std::copy instead of a raw loop" over an etl::vector with a
# fixed capacity.  The loop is three lines and says what it does; the algorithm
# call would not be shorter and would not be clearer.
useStlAlgorithm

# Anything the dependency tree or a build directory drags in.
*:*/_deps/*
*:*/build/*
*:*/build-*/*
